module v4.extdeps.languages.typescript


// `Bool` is kernel-ambient (STRUCTURE.md:147). `type TsBoolean = Bool`
// references std/logic.dag's `Bool` without an `import` — correct alias-
// identity, not hollow.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (D2 slice)
//
// ECMAScript partitions `number` (IEEE-754 binary64) and `bigint`
// (exact integers, unbounded) as DISTINCT primitives — not Rust's `i32`
// fixed-width ladder. Structural typing, excess property checks, and
// conditional types are **out of D2** (DECISIONS.md D2 scope guard).


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(2) — GROUNDING MAP (🟡 ENTIRE FACET DEFERRED — operator-pending)
//
// Per mgr brief msg_6d3a3eb2: `GroundingMap` is SHARED with no pinned P2
// home yet. Declaring a local `GroundingMap` in each language file would
// be N parallel declarations — forbidden. **Defer** the carrier type AND
// every `data ts_*_grounding` instance row until the operator pins the
// shared `GroundingMap` authority (escalation path). Includes deferred
// `boolean` / `number` / `bigint` keyword grounding data.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Primitive vocabulary — ECMAScript numeric surface (Handbook + ECMA-262)
//
// TypeScript inherits ECMAScript's two numeric primitives: `number` and
// `bigint` (distinct from Rust's signed/unsigned fixed-width family).
//
// Spec: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//       (sections on `number`, `bigint`)
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-number-type
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-bigint-type
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: both kinds are shared classifiers for every
//      consumer that dispatches on numeric primitive kind.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: nullary tags from a closed ECMA-262
//      partition; a `Bool` proxy would be the M4 numeric/boolean-proxy smell.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: each kind's algebra is std/ (float vs
//      integer chains) reached via **future** D2a(1) aliases, not by
//      collapsing this enum into those carriers.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a value is exactly ONE numeric primitive kind.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: `number` and `bigint` are distinct
//      ECMA primitives, not one indexed family (Practice 7).
type TsEcma262NumericPrimitiveKind
  = TsNumberPrimitive
  | TsBigIntPrimitive


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(1) — alias-identity (kernel-ambient `Bool`)


// ECMAScript / TypeScript `boolean` ↔ std/logic.dag `Bool`.
// Spec: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-boolean-type
type TsBoolean = Bool


// D2a(3) — **omitted** for `boolean`: no ECMA-262 operation-semantics event
// distinct from `BooleanAlgebra<Bool>` (std/logic.dag); no parallel
// overflow / NaN carrier.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(3) — ECMA-262 primitive operation-semantics (TS-native; NOT Rust int
// overflow)
//
// ECMA-262 exposes three **distinct** primitive-semantics obligations the
// resolver must not conflate:
//   (1) `Number` — additive / multiplicative / division / remainder follows
//       IEEE-754 binary64 (NaN / ±∞ propagation), not fixed-width int wrap.
//       Spec: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-numeric-types-number-type
//   (2) `Number` — bitwise operators use ToInt32 / ToUint32; results are
//       integers mod 2³² (a different spec surface from (1)).
//       Spec: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-numberbitwiseop
//   (3) `BigInt` — exact unbounded integers; invalid ops throw per ECMA-262,
//       not silent modular wrap on a Rust-style fixed width.
//       Spec: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-bigint-type
//
// v2-compiler parses `type T = V` (no `|`) as a **type alias** to an
// existing type `V`. A `Disj` therefore needs ≥2 variants joined by `|`.
// The three obligations above are one closed coproduct (not Rust's
// Panic|Wrap axis).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every numeric / emit consumer reads the same
//      three-way partition when dispatching ECMA primitive semantics.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: nullary tags from a closed ECMA-262
//      obligation set; no Bool / numeric proxy.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: IEEE-754 / `Int` bodies land in std/
//      (float.dag / integer.dag) + D2b `Arrow` realizations; this `Disj`
//      names which ECMA track applies at the resolver boundary.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a resolver row selects exactly ONE semantics
//      track per modeled obligation site (mutually exclusive classifier
//      rows, not simultaneous coordinates on one value).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: the three are not `Semantics<Width>` /
//      Practice-7 projection over a declared width set.
type TsEcma262PrimitiveOperationSemantics
  = TsNumberIeee754Binary64Semantics
  | TsNumberBitwiseInt32Uint32Semantics
  | TsBigIntExactUnboundedSemantics


// (No `data` rows — M1(2.8) opaque-body discipline on enum literals until the
// class-5 structural-validation gap closes; the **type** is the D2a(3) carrier.)


